---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../../components/Disclaimer.astro';
import { BUSINESS, MEDICARE_2026 } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'High-Deductible Medicare Supplement Insurance (Plan G)';
const description = 'High-Deductible Plan G is a Medigap plan with the same benefits as standard Plan G but a lower premium and higher deductible. Learn how it works and whether it fits your situation.';
const today = '2026-06-03';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'Service', name: 'High-Deductible Medicare Supplement Plan G', serviceType: 'Medicare Supplement Insurance', provider: { '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/#organization` }, areaServed: [{ '@type': 'State', name: 'New York' }, { '@type': 'State', name: 'Connecticut' }], description },
    { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/services/high-deductible-medicare-supplement#webpage`, name: title, speakable: { '@type': 'SpeakableSpecification', cssSelector: ['.lead', 'h2'] } },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <PageHero
    title="High-Deductible Medicare Supplement Insurance"
    subtitle="The same coverage as standard Plan G — at a lower monthly premium. Here's how it works and who it fits."
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Medicare Plans', href: '/services' }, { label: 'High-Deductible Medigap' }]}
  />

  <div class="bg-crst-light border-b border-navy-100">
    <div class="container-wide py-3 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-2 sm:gap-4 text-center">
      <span class="text-sm font-heading text-navy-700">Not sure if the numbers work for you?</span>
      <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneClean}`} class="btn-accent text-sm px-5 py-2">Call {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="py-14 lg:py-18">
    <div class="container-narrow prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-crst-primary prose-a:text-crst-accent">

      <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-crst-gold bg-navy-50 p-5">
        <p class="text-navy-800 leading-relaxed m-0">
          <strong>High-Deductible Plan G</strong> is a Medicare Supplement (Medigap) plan with the same standardized benefits
          as regular Plan G, but with a lower monthly premium and a higher annual deductible — <strong>{MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} in {MEDICARE_2026.year}</strong>.
          When you use care, you cover the costs Original Medicare leaves behind — its deductibles, copays, and coinsurance —
          out of your own pocket. Those amounts add up toward your annual deductible. Once you reach it, the plan takes over,
          exactly like a standard supplement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="lead text-xl text-navy-700">
        With High-Deductible Plan G, your total annual out-of-pocket is your lower annual premium plus the {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible}
        deductible — and for many people, even that amount compares favorably to a full year of standard Plan G premiums. You
        trade a lower monthly premium for a higher deductible. You only pay if you actually need care. Most people do not reach
        the full deductible every year, so they often come out ahead on total annual cost.
      </p>

      <h2>How does High-Deductible Plan G work?</h2>
      <p>Here's the trade-off:</p>

      <div class="not-prose grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-crst-primary p-5 text-white">
          <h3 class="font-heading font-semibold text-crst-gold mb-3 mt-0">High-Deductible Plan G</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-white/85 list-none p-0 m-0">
            <li>• Lower monthly premium</li>
            <li>• You pay covered costs up to {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} ({MEDICARE_2026.year})</li>
            <li>• Can be a lower total annual cost compared with Standard Plan G</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy-100 bg-navy-50 p-5">
          <h3 class="font-heading font-semibold text-crst-primary mb-3 mt-0">Standard Plan G</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-navy-600 list-none p-0 m-0">
            <li>• Higher monthly premium</li>
            <li>• Lower out-of-pocket costs once Part B deductible is met</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>With the high-deductible option, here's what you retain</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Original Medicare remains primary.</li>
        <li>You can generally use any provider nationwide who accepts Medicare.</li>
        <li>There is no provider network.</li>
        <li>Referrals are generally not required.</li>
        <li>After the {MEDICARE_2026.year} deductible of {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} is reached, high-deductible Plan G provides the standardized Plan G benefits for the remainder of the calendar year.</li>
        <li>The deductible applies to Medicare-approved cost-sharing — not the provider's full retail bill. The result is that you're managing the total cost of Medicare coverage over time.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who does the high-deductible plan make the most sense for?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Those who want to reduce monthly expenses while keeping real protection</li>
        <li>People who are generally healthy or comfortable with some financial risk</li>
        <li>Those who prefer a cost-efficient, long-term strategy</li>
        <li>People who live in a state (like New York or Connecticut) where you can change plans later with no underwriting</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Which plan is more appropriate? It depends on where you live, how much care you expect to use, and how you prefer to
        manage cost. See the full side-by-side in <a href="/high-deductible-plan-g-vs-plan-g">High-Deductible Plan G vs. standard Plan G</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Can you switch out of a High-Deductible Plan later?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes — however, where you live decides how easily. In New York and
        Connecticut, you can switch Medigap plans any time of year with no health questions and no underwriting, so moving
        off a high-deductible plan later is straightforward. If you switch mid-year, be aware that your deductible would
        reset to zero.
      </p>
      <p>
        In most other states, switching after your initial 6-month Medigap window usually requires medical underwriting, and
        you could be declined. We cover the details in <a href="/switch-high-deductible-plan-g-to-plan-g">switching out of High-Deductible Plan G</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl bg-crst-primary p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-white font-heading text-lg mb-2 m-0">Not sure if the numbers work for you?</p>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mb-4 m-0">I'll compare your real total annual cost across plans — no cost, no pressure.</p>
        <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phoneClean}`} class="btn-accent text-base px-7 py-3">Call {BUSINESS.phone}</a>
      </div>

      <h2>Go deeper on High-Deductible Plan G</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/high-deductible-plan-g-worth-it">Is a High-Deductible Plan Worth it...the Pros &amp; Cons</a></li>
        <li><a href="/high-deductible-plan-g-vs-plan-g">High-Deductible Plan G vs. standard Plan G</a></li>
        <li><a href="/switch-high-deductible-plan-g-to-plan-g">Can you switch out of High-Deductible Plan G later?</a></li>
        <li><a href="/high-deductible-plan-f-vs-plan-g">High-Deductible Plan F vs. High-Deductible Plan G</a></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="not-prose mt-8">
        <Disclaimer variant="tpmo" />
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          High-Deductible Plan G involves higher out-of-pocket costs before coverage begins and is not suitable for everyone.
          The {MEDICARE_2026.hdDeductible} figure is the {MEDICARE_2026.year} deductible set by Medicare and changes annually.
          NY producer license #: {BUSINESS.nyLicense}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection headline="Let's see if the numbers work for your situation." />
</BaseLayout>
